#### Problem 1: Service Endpoint Proliferation and Discovery

**Scenario: Provider Portal Service Endpoint Management**

Gainwell Provider+™ portal dashboard requires data from 10+ backend services. In a direct service-to-service model:

```javascript
// Provider Portal Configuration - Service Endpoints
const serviceEndpoints = {
  providerService: process.env.PROVIDER_SERVICE_URL || 'https://provider-svc-1a2b3c.eastus.cloudapp.azure.com:8443',
  credentialingService: process.env.CREDENTIALING_SERVICE_URL || 'https://credentialing-svc-4d5e6f.eastus.cloudapp.azure.com:8443',
  claimsService: process.env.CLAIMS_SERVICE_URL || 'https://claims-svc-7g8h9i.eastus.cloudapp.azure.com:8443',
  paymentsService: process.env.PAYMENTS_SERVICE_URL || 'https://payments-svc-j1k2l3.eastus.cloudapp.azure.com:8443',
  priorAuthService: process.env.PRIORAUTH_SERVICE_URL || 'https://priorauth-svc-m4n5o6.eastus.cloudapp.azure.com:8443',
  // ... 5 more services
};

// Each service requires separate connection, DNS lookup, TLS handshake
// Kubernetes deployments change pod IPs requiring configuration updates
// No automatic health checks or failover
```

**Problems:**
- **Configuration Complexity**: 10+ environment variables per application × 50+ applications = 500+ configuration entries
- **DNS Management**: Each service requires DNS entry, SSL certificate, firewall rules
- **Dynamic Endpoints**: Kubernetes pod IPs change with deployments, scaling, failures—requiring dynamic discovery
- **Cross-Region Routing**: No intelligent routing to closest/healthiest region (East vs. Central vs. West)
- **Development Environment**: Developers must run 10+ services locally or maintain complex remote connection configurations

