### Example 1: Provider Portal API Consolidation

**Context**: Gainwell's Provider+™ portal requires data from 12 different backend microservices (provider demographics, credentialing status, claims history, payments, prior authorizations, messages, alerts, documents, training records, contracts, performance metrics, support tickets). Previously, the portal's frontend made direct calls to each service, resulting in complex client-side logic, security token management across 12 services, and difficulty handling service failures.

**Before Implementation:**

```typescript
// Frontend code - Provider Dashboard (Before Gateway)
class ProviderDashboard {
  async loadDashboard(providerId: string) {
    try {
      // Separate API calls to 12 different services
      const [
        provider,
        credentialing,
        claims,
        payments,
        priorAuths,
        messages,
        alerts,
        documents,
        training,
        contracts,
        metrics,
        tickets
      ] = await Promise.all([
        fetch(`https://provider-service.gainwell.com/api/providers/${providerId}`, {
          headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${this.getToken('provider-service')}` }
        }),
        fetch(`https://credentialing-service.gainwell.com/api/credentials/${providerId}`, {
          headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${this.getToken('credentialing-service')}` }
        }),
        fetch(`https://claims-service.gainwell.com/api/claims?providerId=${providerId}&limit=10`, {
          headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${this.getToken('claims-service')}` }
        }),
        // ... 9 more similar fetch calls
      ]);

      return {
        provider: await provider.json(),
        credentialing: await credentialing.json(),
        claims: await claims.json(),
        // ... process 9 more responses
      };
    } catch (error) {
      // Complex error handling for each service
      console.error('Dashboard load failed:', error);
    }
  }

  private getToken(service: string): string {
    // Maintain separate tokens for each service
    return this.tokenCache[service] || this.refreshToken(service);
  }
}
```

**Problems Encountered:**
- Frontend maintains 12 different OAuth tokens, each with separate expiration times
- Network overhead: 12 separate HTTPS connections, DNS lookups, TLS handshakes
- Error handling complexity: 12 potential failure points requiring separate retry logic
- Security risk: 12 service URLs exposed to client, tokens visible in browser dev tools
- Performance: Serial authentication flow adds 3-5 seconds to initial page load
- Maintenance burden: URL changes require frontend redeployment

**After Implementation (with API Gateway):**

```typescript
// Frontend code - Provider Dashboard (After Gateway)
class ProviderDashboard {
  private gatewayUrl = 'https://api.gainwell.com';
  private token: string; // Single OAuth token for gateway

  async loadDashboard(providerId: string) {
    try {
      // Single API call to gateway - all data aggregated backend
      const response = await fetch(
        `${this.gatewayUrl}/api/v1/providers/${providerId}/dashboard`,
        {
          headers: {
            'Authorization': `Bearer ${this.token}`,
            'X-Client-Version': '2.1.0'
          }
        }
      );

      if (!response.ok) {
        throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}: ${response.statusText}`);
      }

      return await response.json(); // Aggregated dashboard data
    } catch (error) {
      // Centralized error handling
      this.handleGatewayError(error);
    }
  }

  private handleGatewayError(error: Error) {
    // Gateway returns standardized error format (RFC 7807)
    if (error.message.includes('401')) {
      this.refreshToken();
    } else if (error.message.includes('429')) {
      this.showRateLimitMessage();
    } else {
      this.showGenericError();
    }
  }
}
```

**Gateway Routing Configuration:**

```xml
<!-- Azure APIM Policy -->
<policies>
  <inbound>
    <base />
    <!-- Validate single OAuth token -->
    <validate-jwt header-name="Authorization">
      <openid-config url="https://login.microsoftonline.com/{tenant}/.well-known/openid-configuration" />
    </validate-jwt>

    <!-- Route to provider service -->
    <set-backend-service base-url="https://provider-service.internal" />

    <!-- Add correlation ID for tracing -->
    <set-header name="X-Correlation-ID" exists-action="override">
      <value>@(Guid.NewGuid().ToString())</value>
    </set-header>
  </inbound>
  <backend>
    <base />
  </backend>
  <outbound>
    <!-- Cache dashboard data for 5 minutes -->
    <cache-store duration="300" />
    <base />
  </outbound>
  <on-error>
    <!-- Return standardized error response -->
    <return-response>
      <set-status code="@(context.Response.StatusCode)" />
      <set-body>@{
        return new JObject(
          new JProperty("type", "https://api.gainwell.com/errors/gateway-error"),
          new JProperty("title", "Gateway Error"),
          new JProperty("status", context.Response.StatusCode),
          new JProperty("traceId", context.RequestId)
        ).ToString();
      }</set-body>
    </return-response>
  </on-error>
</policies>
```

**Results:**
- **Frontend Code Reduction**: 70% less code (removed 12 separate API clients, token managers, error handlers)
- **Performance Improvement**: Dashboard load time reduced from 4.2s to 1.8s (57% faster)
- **Security Enhancement**: Single OAuth token, backend service URLs no longer exposed to client
- **Developer Velocity**: New dashboard widgets added without frontend changes (backend aggregation)
- **Operational Simplicity**: Single monitoring endpoint for dashboard data, unified error handling
- **Cache Hit Rate**: 65% of dashboard requests served from cache (5-minute TTL)

**Metrics (30 days post-implementation):**

| Metric | Before Gateway | After Gateway | Improvement |
|--------|---------------|---------------|-------------|
| Page Load Time (p95) | 4.2s | 1.8s | 57% faster |
| API Call Count | 12 per load | 1 per load | 92% reduction |
| Frontend Code (LoC) | 1,850 lines | 560 lines | 70% reduction |
| Auth Token Management | 12 tokens | 1 token | 92% reduction |
| Error Rate | 3.2% | 0.8% | 75% reduction |
| Support Tickets | 45/month | 12/month | 73% reduction |
